 (delivery-scope
  . "W7 blocked-wave repair, bake and v1.00.31 release, in three parts. PART 1 — the v1.00.30 W4 wave repaired and delivered under issue 9690: campaign/v1.00.30-w4 squash-merged as cc25b3663362d032b9a23a9d22f9dd5edbe637d8 (PR 9752, 22/22 required checks green) after 12 independent review rounds ending APPROVED with no non-blocking observations, binding publication 5f4a80fcda0c80396ca033184ae085139f02002c (PR 9753, EMPTY_SHA publication diff over exactly the three record files, record-commit pure, binding review APPROVED), main run 36087264560 concluded success, governance governed, sync synchronized, status delivered, issue 9690 closed as completed and board Done. PART 2 — the v1.00.31 bake: util/version.rkt 1.00.29 to 1.00.31 as the single source of truth, with info.rkt/README.md/docs synced by canonical generators only (sync-version.rkt --write --all, lint-doc-freshness.rkt --fix, sync-readme-status.rkt --sync, metrics.rkt --sync-all); v1.00.30 is skipped because it never shipped a tag. PART 3 — what the bake found, which is the substance of this wave. The first verification chain that actually measured this worktree found and fixed a defect in the test runner itself: resolve-base-dir in scripts/run-tests/classify-metadata.rkt tried q-shaped candidates before the launch tree, so a runner launched in any worktree beside a q/ clone silently measured that clone and printed a RUN-SUMMARY naming the clone's version. Every earlier local suite run had been misdirected, which is why none of the following could have been found. With the fix and 4 regression tests, three classes of defect surfaced, all correct on main only while q-version happened to be 1.00.29: (a) 8 test files derived FROZEN v1.00.29-campaign artifact paths from the live version and are now pinned literally with the reason recorded, while the tier-ownership matrix stays derived because it is a current-tree drift check and this milestone's copy was regenerated by the canonical generator; (b) 2 files unchanged from base had the mirror defect, a derived value that is a frozen authoring identity (the shard-plan report's wave field, which the committed example artifact pairs with its own spec_reference, and the v1.00.29 final-cohort directory, a frozen measurement this bake did not reproduce) and are now pinned; (c) tests/test-worker-security.rkt could not fail the gate at all, because its W2 overlap checks ran as module-body cases after the file's first run-tests, so their failures never reached the process exit code that the runner reads, and it was hiding class (a) in its own lane. It now runs those checks through run-tests, whose failure count drives the exit, with red-first proof. Making that check able to run also exposed a fifth pre-existing failure, a strict-runner assertion pinned to the literal pre-W4 invocation shape that this campaign's own W4 compiled-root repair had legitimately changed. Two coherence repairs followed: the bake's own BUG-0009 sweep had invalidated 2 of the 9 digest-bound W6 rehearsal inputs, so the matrix was regenerated by its canonical generator, its head re-stamped to the last published commit, SHA256SUMS rebound, and the report sentence claiming an unchanged inputs digest replaced with the truth; and the W4-retained local capture's four runner-suite sections are corrected in w4-recovery.json, with a true re-measurement of the W4 head retained and W4's authoritative CI gates stated as unaffected. The annotated tag v1.00.31 is pushed only after this wave merges, main CI is green, and the readiness gate plus the full CI-strict tag-publish preflight pass on clean main."))
